Z||000003||BBBAD GT||07-09-2001||09:33 AM||||That Fiero is a local one around me.  The guy (a real nice guy) works for the boating industry, and obtained his 350 from Mercruiser.  I believe he used the archie kit, or some form of it because he did alot of the custom work himself, like making brackets to use the 4 cyl water pump off the side of the engine like an accessory.  The car runs good, and he applied the 'boat theme' inside if you ever look at his interior.  <P>One thing about the motor tho, for boats, the weight of the motor doesn't come into play as much as in a car, so most boat manifolds/heads/block is made of iron to be less likely to rust and is cheaper.  So I have no idea how much extra his motor weights, but only to say it doesn't sag in the rear with his stock springs (I can't understand that).<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
